(Project Objectives:) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(  * Autonomous Role Decomposition: Segment complex trip planning into bounded,) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(    single-responsibility agent roles \(Manager, Destination, Budget, Weather, Critic\).) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(  * Strict Schema Enforcement: Guarantee 100% valid JSON responses using Zod) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(    runtime validation and Groq strict JSON-schema decoding.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(  * Deterministic Arithmetic Integrity: Compute all distance calculations) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(    \(Haversine trigonometric formulas\) and budget summations strictly in TypeScript) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(    to prevent LLM hallucination.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(  * Closed-Loop Adversarial Critique: Deploy an independent Critic Agent capable) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(    of rejecting inadequate drafts and commanding targeted agent revisions.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(  * Production-Grade Resilience: Implement dynamic multi-model failover, 404 model) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(    pruning, round-robin multi-key pooling, and guaranteed offline fallback.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(  * Transparent Auditability: Record every inter-agent message, tool call, latency,) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(    and decision in a monotonic execution trace exportable in JSON format.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
() Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(4. SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE & AUTONOMOUS AGENTS) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(TripNexus orchestrates five specialized agents coordinated by a centralized) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(orchestrator and an immutable monotonic execution ledger:) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
() Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(1. Trip Manager Agent \(trip_manager\):) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Serves as the executive planner and state supervisor.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Validates user inputs \(dates, origin, destination, group size, budget, pace\).) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Deconstructs planning goals into structured assignments for specialists.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Intercepts Critic rejections, increments revision counters, and dispatches) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(     targeted revision tickets to responsible agents \(bounded at 3 cycles\).) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
() Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(2. Destination Specialist Agent \(destination_agent\):) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Selects points of interest strictly from a verified 11-city catalog.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Clusters activities geographically by city area to minimize travel fatigue.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Executes local tools \(places_search, place_details, route_distance\).) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Computes straight-line distances using the Haversine trigonometric formula:) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(       d = 2 * R * asin\(sqrt\(sin^2\(dLat/2\) + cos\(lat1\)*cos\(lat2\)*sin^2\(dLon/2\)\)\)) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
() Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(3. Budget Assessor Agent \(budget_agent\):) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Operates on deterministic local calculations: accommodation, food, activities,) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(     local transit, and a 10% contingency reserve for the full traveler group.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Explains cost drivers, headroom, and financial trade-offs in clear text.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Never fabricates arithmetic; LLM reasoning is strictly explanatory.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
() Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(4. Climate & Seasonality Specialist \(weather_agent\):) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Queries verified historical climate records for the destination and month.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Computes rain probability, typical temperature ranges \(Celsius\), and season tags.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Flags high-risk outdoor activities \(>= 50% rain probability\) and suggests) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(     verified indoor alternatives from the destination catalog.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
() Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(5. Independent Critic Agent \(critic_agent\):) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Operates as an adversarial auditor evaluating the consolidated itinerary draft.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Evaluates four non-negotiable criteria:) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(       a\) Date Continuity  : Validates sequential, unbroken day-by-day dates.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
