0 -13.5 Td
(5. CLOSED-LOOP REPLANNING & CONFLICT RESOLUTION) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(When the Critic Agent discovers a constraint violation:) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(  Step 1: Critic outputs decision: "REJECTED" with structured issue descriptions.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(  Step 2: Trip Manager intercepts the rejection, increments revisionCount, and) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(          translates issues into a targeted revision prompt.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(  Step 3: Responsible specialist \(e.g., Destination or Budget Agent\) re-executes,) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(          adjusting activities, substituting indoor venues, or rebalancing costs.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(  Step 4: Revised itinerary draft is re-submitted to the Critic Agent for audit.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(  Step 5: The loop terminates upon Critic APPROVAL or upon reaching the 3-cycle) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(          safety bound, preventing infinite loops and runaway API costs.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(  Step 6: If minor warnings remain after 3 cycles, the itinerary is tagged with) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(          an amber "NEEDS ATTENTION" status badge so the traveler can review caveats.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
() Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(6. KEY TECHNICAL INNOVATIONS & RECENT RESILIENCE UPGRADES) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(TripNexus introduces several state-of-the-art resilience capabilities:) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
() Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(A. Multi-Model Failover Pool:) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Leverages Groq Cloud LPU acceleration with sub-second inference speeds.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Primary inference runs on openai/gpt-oss-120b.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Dynamic fallback cascade: openai/gpt-oss-120b -> qwen/qwen3.8-27b ->) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(     openai/gpt-oss-20b.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
() Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(B. Dynamic 404 Model Pruning:) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Automatically intercepts HTTP 404 \("model not available to this account"\)) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(     responses from provider endpoints.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Prunes unavailable models dynamically from the candidate pool during runtime,) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(     preventing redundant failed attempts and preserving true rate-limit attribution.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
() Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(C. Multi-Key Round-Robin Rotation:) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Auto-discovers and pools multiple Groq API keys \(comma-separated or named) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(     variables like TripNexus2, TripNexus3, TripNexus4, TripNexus5\).) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Distributes load across all keys, multiplying free-tier capacity to) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(     120 RPM \(Requests Per Minute\) and 32,000 TPM \(Tokens Per Minute\).) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * Automatically switches keys upon encountering 429 rate limits or quota drops.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
() Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(D. Stateless Serverless Trace Delivery:) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * In Vercel serverless functions, execution events are bundled directly into) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(     the primary plan result payload.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(   * The client renders all 120+ execution trace events immediately, preventing) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(     secondary 404 race conditions common in stateless serverless environments.) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
() Tj
0 -13.5 Td
(E. Guaranteed Zero-Crash Offline Fallback:) Tj
0 -13.5 Td
